 "title": "Min-stacks and monotonic queues",
 "short": "Min-stacks and monotonic queues",
 "lead": "An Essential section on a stack and a queue that report their smallest element in constant time, on using such a queue to find the minimum of every window of fixed length, and on finding each element’s nearest smaller value with a stack. The largest all-zero submatrix is Advanced. cp-algorithms counts from 0 (A[0] to A[N − 1], rows 0 to n − 1); Wikipedia’s A[1..n] counts from 1, with a sentinel A[0].",
