 "exercise_notes": "ODS’s Exercises 3.15 (MinQueue) and 3.16 (MinDeque) ask for a design in words and have no tests, so they are not set. TheAlgorithms’ queue_by_two_stacks, monotonic_queue, sliding_window_maximum, stock_span_problem, next_greater_element and largest_rectangle_histogram, tryalgo’s our_queue and keon’s max_sliding_window carry tests but print no exercise statement, so they have no card. Interactive Coding Challenges’ stack_min and queue_from_stacks are left out: the first loses a repeated minimum and the second moves every element back on each enqueue, which is quadratic. Kattis’s bungeebuilder is left for a later pass, and keon’s heap version of the window waits for the heaps of chapter 9. MIT 6.046J’s “Extreme FIFO Queues”, which chapter 1’s plan had placed in 1.5, is set here with the NC cards.",
