   "cite": "min-stack",
   "changes": "The tests call run(ops), which the starter defines: it plays a list of operations on a new MinStack and returns what pop, size and min return. Its first two tests are TheAlgorithms’ doctests for stack_tracking_min_max.py (MIT, © The Algorithms), less the size limit and the value they return on an empty stack, which the exercise does not ask for; min and pop are never called on an empty stack.",
   "prompt": "Design and implement a <code>MinStack</code> data structure that can store comparable elements and supports the stack operations <code>push(x)</code>, <code>pop()</code>, and <code>size()</code>, as well as the <code>min()</code> operation, which returns the minimum value currently stored in the data structure. All operations should run in constant time.",
